sequenceDiagram
    participant PM as Project Manager/SPOC
    participant UI as E4H Web UI (Extended)
    participant GW as E4H API Gateway (Existing)
    participant AUTH as E4H Auth Service (Existing)
    participant HRMS as eGov HRMS (Existing)
    participant AMS as Activity Management Service (NEW)
    participant FPS as Field Planner Service (NEW)
    participant EGOV_FS as eGov Filestore (Existing)
    participant DB as E4H PostgreSQL (Shared)
    participant QUEUE as Kafka Queue (Shared)
    participant NEW_USER as New User
    
    Note over PM,NEW_USER: E4H Integrated User Management via eGov HRMS
    
    PM->>UI: Navigate to Team Management (E4H UI)
    UI->>GW: GET /user/oauth/me
    GW->>AUTH: Validate PM/SPOC JWT token
    AUTH->>HRMS: GET /egov-hrms/employees/_search
    Note over AUTH,HRMS: Validate PM has team management permissions
    HRMS-->>AUTH: PM validated with team management role
    AUTH-->>GW: User authenticated
    GW-->>UI: User authenticated
    
    UI->>GW: GET /egov-hrms/employees/_search?supervisorId={pmId}
    GW->>HRMS: Get team members for PM/SPOC (existing service)
    HRMS->>DB: Query eg_hrms_employee and eg_hrms_assignment tables
    DB-->>HRMS: Return team member list with assignments
    HRMS-->>GW: Return team data
    GW-->>UI: Display team dashboard
    UI-->>PM: Show current team members and roles
    
    PM->>UI: Click "Add Team Member"
    Note over PM,UI: Redirects to eGov HRMS employee management
    Note over UI: Field Planner integrates with existing E4H user management
    Note over UI: Uses eGov HRMS for all employee operations
    
    alt Single Employee Creation (via eGov HRMS)
        PM->>UI: Fill employee creation form
        Note over PM,UI: Name, Phone, Employee Type, Department, Designation
        
        PM->>UI: Submit employee creation form
        UI->>GW: POST /egov-hrms/employees/_create
        GW->>HRMS: Create new employee (existing service)
        
        HRMS->>DB: Check if employee already exists (eg_hrms_employee table)
        alt Employee Already Exists
            DB-->>HRMS: Return duplicate error
            HRMS-->>GW: Return validation error
            GW-->>UI: Show error message
            UI-->>PM: "Employee with this phone/code already exists"
        else Employee Details Valid
            HRMS->>DB: Begin transaction
            HRMS->>DB: Create eg_hrms_employee record
            DB-->>HRMS: Return employee UUID
            
            HRMS->>DB: Create eg_hrms_assignment record
            Note over HRMS,DB: Link employee to PM as supervisor
            DB-->>HRMS: Assignment created
            
            HRMS->>DB: Commit transaction
            DB-->>HRMS: Employee created successfully
            
            Note over HRMS: E4H audit patterns handle employee creation logging
            
            Note over HRMS: E4H notification system handles onboarding
            HRMS->>QUEUE: Publish EmployeeCreatedEvent
            
            HRMS-->>GW: Employee created successfully
            GW-->>UI: Return success response
            UI-->>PM: Show "Employee created and assigned to your team"
        end
        
    else Bulk Employee Creation via Excel (E4H Integration)
        PM->>UI: Click "Bulk Create Employees"
        UI->>GW: GET /field-planner/v1/employees/bulk-template
        GW->>AMS: Generate bulk creation template (Field Planner service)
        AMS->>EGOV_FS: POST /filestore/v1/files (generate template)
        EGOV_FS-->>AMS: Return Excel template UUID and URL
        AMS-->>GW: Return template download link
        GW-->>UI: Download template from eGov Filestore
        UI-->>PM: Template downloaded
        
        PM->>PM: Fill employee data in Excel template
        PM->>UI: Upload completed employee file
        
        UI->>GW: POST /field-planner/v1/employees/bulk-create (multipart)
        GW->>AMS: Process bulk employee creation (new service)
        AMS->>EGOV_FS: POST /filestore/v1/files (validate uploaded file)
        EGOV_FS->>EGOV_FS: Validate Excel format
        
        alt Invalid Excel Format
            EGOV_FS-->>AMS: Return format error
            AMS-->>GW: Return format error
            GW-->>UI: Show format error
            UI-->>PM: "Invalid file format, use template"
        else Valid Format
            EGOV_FS->>EGOV_FS: Parse employee data
            EGOV_FS-->>AMS: Return employee list
            
            AMS->>HRMS: POST /egov-hrms/employees/_create (bulk)
            Note over AMS,HRMS: Use existing eGov HRMS bulk creation capability
            HRMS->>DB: Process employee creation in bulk
            
            loop For each employee
                HRMS->>DB: Validate employee data (eg_hrms_employee table)
                HRMS->>HRMS: Check employee uniqueness
                HRMS->>HRMS: Validate phone number format
                
                Note over HRMS: eGov HRMS handles all employee validations
                Note over HRMS: Creates eg_hrms_employee and eg_hrms_assignment records
                Note over HRMS: Publishes EmployeeCreatedEvent via Kafka
                Note over HRMS: E4H audit patterns handle bulk creation logging
                US->>US: Validate role assignments
                
                alt Validation Error
                    US->>US: Add to error list
                else Valid User
                    US->>US: Add to valid users list
                end
            end
            
            alt Validation Errors Found
                US->>US: Generate error report
                US-->>API: Return bulk creation errors
                API-->>UI: Show error summary
                UI-->>PM: "Some users failed validation, download error report"
                
            else All Users Valid
                US->>DB: Begin transaction
                
                loop For each valid user
                    US->>DB: Create user record
                    DB-->>US: Return user ID
                    
                    US->>AUTH: Generate verification token
                    AUTH-->>US: Return token
                    US->>DB: Store verification token
                    
                    US->>DB: Create team association
                    DB-->>US: Association created
                    
                    US->>NS: Queue verification email
                end
                
                US->>DB: Commit transaction
                DB-->>US: All users created
                
                US->>AS: Log bulk creation audit
                AS->>DB: Store audit record
                DB-->>AS: Audit logged
                
                NS->>EMAIL: Send all verification emails
                loop For each new user
                    EMAIL->>NEW_USER: Send verification email
                end
                
                US-->>API: Bulk creation successful
                API-->>UI: Return success summary
                UI-->>PM: Show "X users created successfully"
            end
        end
    end
    
    Note over PM,NEW_USER: User Verification Process
    
    NEW_USER->>EMAIL: Receive verification email
    NEW_USER->>NEW_USER: Click verification link
    
    NEW_USER->>API: GET /api/v1/auth/verify-email/{token}
    API->>AUTH: Verify email token
    AUTH->>DB: Validate token and check expiry
    
    alt Token Invalid or Expired
        DB-->>AUTH: Return token error
        AUTH-->>API: Return verification error
        API-->>NEW_USER: Show "Invalid or expired verification link"
        
    else Token Valid
        DB-->>AUTH: Token valid
        AUTH->>DB: Begin transaction
        AUTH->>DB: Update user status to ACTIVE
        AUTH->>DB: Mark email as verified
        AUTH->>DB: Remove verification token
        DB-->>AUTH: User activated
        AUTH->>DB: Commit transaction
        
        AUTH->>AS: Log email verification audit
        AS->>DB: Store audit record
        DB-->>AS: Audit logged
        
        AUTH-->>API: Email verified successfully
        API-->>NEW_USER: Show "Email verified, set password"
        
        NEW_USER->>NEW_USER: Create password
        NEW_USER->>API: POST /api/v1/auth/set-password
        API->>AUTH: Set user password
        AUTH->>AUTH: Hash password
        AUTH->>DB: Store password hash
        DB-->>AUTH: Password set
        
        AUTH-->>API: Password set successfully
        API-->>NEW_USER: Show "Account setup complete"
    end
    
    Note over PM,NEW_USER: Team Member Management
    
    PM->>UI: Manage existing team member
    UI->>API: GET /api/v1/users/{id}
    API->>US: Get user details
    US->>DB: Query user information
    DB-->>US: Return user data
    US-->>API: Return user details
    API-->>UI: Display user profile
    UI-->>PM: Show user details and options
    
    alt Update User Roles
        PM->>UI: Modify user roles
        UI->>API: PUT /api/v1/users/{id}/roles
        API->>US: Update user roles
        
        US->>DB: Begin transaction
        US->>DB: Update user roles
        DB-->>US: Roles updated
        US->>DB: Commit transaction
        
        US->>AS: Log role change audit
        AS->>DB: Store audit record
        DB-->>AS: Audit logged
        
        US->>NS: Send role change notification
        NS->>EMAIL: Send notification to user
        EMAIL->>NEW_USER: Notify of role changes
        
        US-->>API: Roles updated successfully
        API-->>UI: Return success response
        UI-->>PM: Show "User roles updated"
        
    else Deactivate User
        PM->>UI: Click "Deactivate User"
        UI->>API: PUT /api/v1/users/{id}/status
        Note over API: Body: { "status": "INACTIVE" }
        API->>US: Deactivate user
        
        US->>DB: Check for active assignments
        alt User Has Active Assignments
            DB-->>US: Return assignment conflict
            US-->>API: Return deactivation error
            API-->>UI: Show error message
            UI-->>PM: "Cannot deactivate: user has active assignments"
            
        else No Active Assignments
            US->>DB: Begin transaction
            US->>DB: Update user status to INACTIVE
            US->>DB: Revoke active sessions
            DB-->>US: User deactivated
            US->>DB: Commit transaction
            
            US->>AS: Log user deactivation audit
            AS->>DB: Store audit record
            DB-->>AS: Audit logged
            
            US->>NS: Send deactivation notification
            NS->>EMAIL: Notify user of deactivation
            EMAIL->>NEW_USER: Account deactivated notification
            
            US-->>API: User deactivated successfully
            API-->>UI: Return success response
            UI-->>PM: Show "User deactivated"
        end
        
    else Remove from Team
        PM->>UI: Click "Remove from Team"
        UI->>API: DELETE /api/v1/teams/members/{userId}
        API->>US: Remove team association
        
        US->>DB: Check for active assignments in team
        alt User Has Team Assignments
            DB-->>US: Return assignment conflict
            US-->>API: Return removal error
            API-->>UI: Show error message
            UI-->>PM: "Cannot remove: user has active team assignments"
            
        else No Team Assignments
            US->>DB: Remove team association
            DB-->>US: Association removed
            
            US->>AS: Log team removal audit
            AS->>DB: Store audit record
            DB-->>AS: Audit logged
            
            US-->>API: Removed from team successfully
            API-->>UI: Return success response
            UI-->>PM: Show "User removed from team"
        end
    end
    
    PM->>UI: View team activity and statistics
    UI->>GW: GET /field-planner/v1/teams/statistics?supervisorId={pmId}
    GW->>AMS: Get team performance data (new service)
    AMS->>HRMS: GET /egov-hrms/employees/_search (get team activity data)
    HRMS->>DB: Query eg_hrms_employee and eg_hrms_assignment for statistics
    DB-->>HRMS: Return team statistics
    HRMS-->>AMS: Return team data
    AMS-->>GW: Return statistics
    GW-->>UI: Display team dashboard
    UI-->>PM: Show team performance metrics
    
    Note over PM,NEW_USER: E4H Platform User Management Integration Complete
    Note over PM,NEW_USER: Field Planner uses eGov HRMS for ALL employee management
    Note over PM,NEW_USER: No duplicate user tables - leverages existing E4H infrastructure  
    Note over PM,NEW_USER: Employee creation, assignment, and team management via eGov HRMS
    Note over PM,NEW_USER: E4H audit patterns and notification system handle all events
    Note over PM,NEW_USER: Consistent with E4H platform conventions and security 